  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_encoder_block(x: list, W_qkv: list, W_ffn1: list, W_ffn2: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Transformer Encoder Block** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np, math\n\ndef dl_encoder_block(x: list, W_qkv: list, W_ffn1: list, W_ffn2: list) -> list:\n    X, S, D = np.array(x, dtype=np.float64), len(x), len(x[0])\n    qkv = np.dot(X, np.array(W_qkv, dtype=np.float64))\n    Q, K, V = qkv[:, :D], qkv[:, D:2*D], qkv[:, 2*D:]\n    sc = np.dot(Q, K.T) / math.sqrt(D)\n    ex = np.exp(sc - np.max(sc, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    attn = np.dot(ex / np.sum(ex, axis=-1, keepdims=True), V)\n    x1 = X + attn; ln1 = (x1 - np.mean(x1, axis=-1, keepdims=True)) / (np.std(x1, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n    ffn = np.dot(np.maximum(0.0, np.dot(ln1, np.array(W_ffn1, dtype=np.float64))), np.array(W_ffn2, dtype=np.float64))\n    x2 = ln1 + ffn; ln2 = (x2 - np.mean(x2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)) / (np.std(x2, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n    return np.round(ln2, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
